---
import Layout from '../layouts/Layout.astro';

const schemaData = {
  "@context": "https://schema.org",
  "@graph": [
    {
      "@type": "TechArticle",
      "@id": "https://site-18-chi.vercel.app/act-run-github-actions-locally-debugging-guide/#article",
      "headline": "Act CLI: Run, Test & Debug GitHub Actions Locally Without Committing",
      "description": "Master local GitHub Actions debugging using the nektos/act CLI. Run workflows inside Docker, map runner images, inject local secrets, and eliminate billable cloud iterations.",
      "url": "https://site-18-chi.vercel.app/act-run-github-actions-locally-debugging-guide/",
      "datePublished": "2026-09-03T10:00:00+00:00",
      "dateModified": "2026-09-06T12:00:00+00:00",
      "author": {
        "@type": "Organization",
        "name": "CIPipelineGraph Engineering Team",
        "url": "https://site-18-chi.vercel.app/"
      }
    }
  ]
};
---

<Layout
  title="Act CLI: Run, Test & Debug GitHub Actions Workflows Locally | CIPipelineGraph"
  description="Comprehensive tutorial on using nektos/act to run and debug GitHub Actions workflows locally inside Docker. Avoid git commit spam, test secrets, and simulate events."
  canonical="https://site-18-chi.vercel.app/act-run-github-actions-locally-debugging-guide/"
  schemaJson={JSON.stringify(schemaData)}
  type="article"
>
  <article class="max-w-4xl mx-auto py-8">
    <!-- Breadcrumb -->
    <nav class="flex items-center space-x-2 text-xs font-mono text-slate-400 mb-6">
      <a href="/" class="hover:text-cyan-400 transition">CIPipelineGraph</a>
      <span>/</span>
      <span class="text-slate-300">Guides</span>
      <span>/</span>
      <span class="text-purple-400">Local GHA Debugging with Act</span>
    </nav>

    <!-- Exactly ONE H1 -->
    <h1 class="text-3xl sm:text-5xl font-black text-white tracking-tight mb-6 leading-tight">
      Act CLI: Run, Test & Debug GitHub Actions Locally Without Committing
    </h1>

    <div class="flex items-center space-x-4 text-xs font-mono text-slate-400 border-b border-slate-800/80 pb-6 mb-8">
      <span>Updated: September 2026</span>
      <span>•</span>
      <span>Reading Time: 13 min</span>
      <span>•</span>
      <span class="text-purple-400">DevOps Tooling & Local Testing</span>
    </div>

    <!-- 45-60 Word Featured Snippet Quick Answer Box with Green Accent Border -->
    <div class="border-l-4 border-emerald-500 bg-emerald-950/20 rounded-r-xl p-5 text-left mb-10 shadow-lg shadow-emerald-950/30 backdrop-blur-sm">
      <div class="flex items-center space-x-2 text-xs font-mono font-bold uppercase tracking-wider text-emerald-400 mb-2">
        <svg class="w-4 h-4 text-emerald-400" viewBox="0 0 20 20" fill="currentColor">
          <path fill-rule="evenodd" d="M10 18a8 8 0 100-16 8 8 0 000 16zm3.707-9.293a1 1 0 00-1.414-1.414L9 10.586 7.707 9.293a1 1 0 00-1.414 1.414l2 2a1 1 0 001.414 0l4-4z" clip-rule="evenodd" />
        </svg>
        <span>Quick Answer • Act CLI Mechanics</span>
      </div>
      <p class="text-sm sm:text-base text-slate-200 leading-relaxed font-normal">
        The open-source nektos/act CLI executes GitHub Actions workflows locally inside Docker containers without triggering billable remote runners or polluting git commit histories. By parsing workflow YAML, mounting workspace directories, and mapping runner environments to standard Docker images, act simulates push, pull_request, and workflow_dispatch events for rapid feedback and secret-protected local pipeline debugging.
      </p>
    </div>

    <!-- Core Content Body -->
    <div class="prose prose-invert max-w-none space-y-10 text-slate-300 text-sm sm:text-base leading-relaxed">

      <!-- Section 1: The Git Commit Anti-Pattern -->
      <section>
        <h2 class="text-2xl font-black text-white tracking-tight mb-4 flex items-center gap-2">
          <span class="text-purple-400 font-mono">01.</span> Ending the "commit -m 'try fixing CI 7'" Anti-Pattern
        </h2>
        <p>
          Every software engineer knows the pain of debugging a misconfigured environment variable, syntax flaw, or bash quotation mismatch in a CI pipeline: pushing a dummy commit, waiting 4 minutes in queue, watching it fail on line 42, and repeating the cycle dozens of times.
        </p>
        <div class="grid grid-cols-1 sm:grid-cols-2 gap-4 my-6 font-mono text-xs">
          <div class="bg-rose-950/20 border border-rose-900/60 p-4 rounded-xl">
            <span class="text-rose-400 font-bold block mb-1">Traditional Remote CI Loop:</span>
            <p class="text-slate-400">Edit YAML &rarr; Git Commit &rarr; Git Push &rarr; Wait in Runner Queue &rarr; Cloud Failure (3-6 mins per cycle). Wastes billable minutes, pollutes branch history.</p>
          </div>
          <div class="bg-emerald-950/20 border border-emerald-900/60 p-4 rounded-xl">
            <span class="text-emerald-400 font-bold block mb-1">Act Local Inner Loop:</span>
            <p class="text-slate-400">Edit YAML &rarr; Run <code class="text-emerald-300">act -j lint</code> &rarr; Instant Docker execution &rarr; Immediate stdout feedback (4-8 seconds). Zero git spam.</p>
          </div>
        </div>
      </section>

      <!-- Section 2: Installation & System Architecture -->
      <section>
        <h2 class="text-2xl font-black text-white tracking-tight mb-4 flex items-center gap-2">
          <span class="text-purple-400 font-mono">02.</span> Installation & System Requirements
        </h2>
        <p>
          <code class="text-purple-300 font-mono">nektos/act</code> requires a running Docker daemon (Docker Desktop, OrbStack, Podman, or native Linux dockerd).
        </p>
        <div class="my-4">
          <div class="bg-slate-950 px-4 py-2 border-t border-x border-slate-800 text-slate-400 rounded-t-lg font-mono text-xs font-bold">
            Terminal Installation Commands
          </div>
<pre is:raw class="bg-[#070B12] border border-slate-800 p-4 rounded-b-lg overflow-x-auto text-slate-200 font-mono text-xs leading-relaxed">
# macOS (Homebrew)
brew install act

# Windows (Winget or Chocolatey)
winget install nektos.act
# or: choco install act-cli

# Linux & WSL2 (Official Install Script)
curl --proto '=https' --tlsv1.2 -sSf https://raw.githubusercontent.com/nektos/act/master/install.sh | sudo bash
</pre>
        </div>
      </section>

      <!-- Section 3: Platform Image Mapping & .actrc -->
      <section>
        <h2 class="text-2xl font-black text-white tracking-tight mb-4 flex items-center gap-2">
          <span class="text-purple-400 font-mono">03.</span> Runner Platform Mapping & .actrc Configuration
        </h2>
        <p>
          By default, <code class="text-slate-200 font-mono">act</code> maps <code class="text-cyan-400 font-mono">ubuntu-latest</code> to a lightweight Docker image. However, official GitHub runners contain hundreds of pre-installed CLI utilities (Docker, AWS CLI, Kubectl, Python, Go, Rust). For maximum fidelity, configure <code class="text-slate-200 font-mono">catthehacker/ubuntu:act-latest</code> in a repository <code class="text-cyan-400 font-mono">.actrc</code> file:
        </p>

        <div class="my-4">
          <div class="bg-slate-950 px-4 py-2 border-t border-x border-slate-800 text-slate-400 rounded-t-lg font-mono text-xs font-bold">
            Project Configuration: .actrc
          </div>
<pre is:raw class="bg-[#070B12] border border-slate-800 p-4 rounded-b-lg overflow-x-auto text-slate-200 font-mono text-xs leading-relaxed">
# Map GitHub Actions runner tags to high-fidelity container images
-P ubuntu-latest=catthehacker/ubuntu:act-latest
-P ubuntu-24.04=catthehacker/ubuntu:act-24.04
-P ubuntu-22.04=catthehacker/ubuntu:act-22.04

# Reuse containers between steps to accelerate runtime
--reuse

# Pass host Docker daemon socket for jobs executing Docker commands
--container-daemon-socket /var/run/docker.sock
</pre>
        </div>

        <div class="overflow-x-auto my-6 border border-slate-800 rounded-xl bg-slate-900/40 font-mono text-xs">
          <table class="w-full text-left border-collapse">
            <thead>
              <tr class="border-b border-slate-800 bg-slate-950 text-slate-300">
                <th class="p-3.5 font-bold">Image Tier</th>
                <th class="p-3.5 font-bold">Docker Hub Image</th>
                <th class="p-3.5 font-bold">Size</th>
                <th class="p-3.5 font-bold">Included Utilities</th>
              </tr>
            </thead>
            <tbody class="divide-y divide-slate-800/60 text-slate-300">
              <tr class="hover:bg-slate-800/20">
                <td class="p-3 font-semibold text-white">Micro Image</td>
                <td class="p-3 text-cyan-400">node:16-buster-slim</td>
                <td class="p-3 text-emerald-400">~200 MB</td>
                <td class="p-3 text-slate-400">Bare Node.js & git only</td>
              </tr>
              <tr class="hover:bg-slate-800/20">
                <td class="p-3 font-semibold text-white">Medium (Default)</td>
                <td class="p-3 text-cyan-400">catthehacker/ubuntu:act-latest</td>
                <td class="p-3 text-amber-400">~2.2 GB</td>
                <td class="p-3 text-slate-300">Python, Node, Docker, Go, Make</td>
              </tr>
              <tr class="hover:bg-slate-800/20">
                <td class="p-3 font-semibold text-white">Full Parity</td>
                <td class="p-3 text-cyan-400">catthehacker/ubuntu:full-latest</td>
                <td class="p-3 text-rose-400">~18 GB</td>
                <td class="p-3 text-slate-300">100% exact GitHub hosted replica</td>
              </tr>
            </tbody>
          </table>
        </div>
      </section>

      <!-- Section 4: Daily Workflows & Command Cheatsheet -->
      <section>
        <h2 class="text-2xl font-black text-white tracking-tight mb-4 flex items-center gap-2">
          <span class="text-purple-400 font-mono">04.</span> Essential Act Commands for Daily Development
        </h2>
        <p>
          Mastering the command syntax empowers developers to target specific jobs, inject local environment variables, and inspect the workflow DAG graph:
        </p>

        <div class="space-y-4 my-4">
          <div>
            <div class="text-xs font-mono font-bold text-white mb-1">1. List All Discovered Workflows and Jobs:</div>
<pre is:raw class="bg-[#070B12] border border-slate-800 p-3 rounded-lg overflow-x-auto text-cyan-300 font-mono text-xs">
act -l
</pre>
          </div>

          <div>
            <div class="text-xs font-mono font-bold text-white mb-1">2. Run a Single Job by Name (Bypassing Full Pipeline):</div>
<pre is:raw class="bg-[#070B12] border border-slate-800 p-3 rounded-lg overflow-x-auto text-cyan-300 font-mono text-xs">
act -j test-unit
</pre>
          </div>

          <div>
            <div class="text-xs font-mono font-bold text-white mb-1">3. Simulate a Pull Request Event with Secrets:</div>
<pre is:raw class="bg-[#070B12] border border-slate-800 p-3 rounded-lg overflow-x-auto text-cyan-300 font-mono text-xs">
act pull_request \
  --secret-file .secrets \
  --var ENVIRONMENT=staging \
  -s GITHUB_TOKEN="$(gh auth token)"
</pre>
          </div>

          <div>
            <div class="text-xs font-mono font-bold text-white mb-1">4. Dry-Run Execution (Validate Syntax & Actions Graph Without Running Steps):</div>
<pre is:raw class="bg-[#070B12] border border-slate-800 p-3 rounded-lg overflow-x-auto text-cyan-300 font-mono text-xs">
act -n
</pre>
          </div>
        </div>
      </section>

      <!-- Section 5: Secrets & Security Safeguards -->
      <section>
        <h2 class="text-2xl font-black text-white tracking-tight mb-4 flex items-center gap-2">
          <span class="text-purple-400 font-mono">05.</span> Local Secrets Management & Security Hygiene
        </h2>
        <p>
          Never hardcode tokens into workflow files or commit them to source control. Create a local <code class="text-slate-200 font-mono">.secrets</code> file in your repository root and ensure it is included in <code class="text-cyan-400 font-mono">.gitignore</code>:
        </p>
        <div class="my-4">
          <div class="bg-slate-950 px-4 py-2 border-t border-x border-slate-800 text-slate-400 rounded-t-lg font-mono text-xs font-bold">
            .secrets (Strictly Git-Ignored)
          </div>
<pre is:raw class="bg-[#070B12] border border-slate-800 p-4 rounded-b-lg overflow-x-auto text-slate-200 font-mono text-xs leading-relaxed">
AWS_ACCESS_KEY_ID=AKIAIOSFODNN7EXAMPLE
AWS_SECRET_ACCESS_KEY=wJalrXUtnFEMI/K7MDENG/bPxRfiCYEXAMPLEKEY
SNYK_AUTH_TOKEN=00000000-0000-0000-0000-000000000000
NPM_TOKEN=npm_mock_token_for_local_ci
</pre>
        </div>
        <p class="text-xs text-slate-400">
          When running act, supply <code class="text-cyan-400 font-mono">--secret-file .secrets</code>. The CLI securely injects these values into the container environment and scrubs them from terminal stdout logs.
        </p>
      </section>

      <!-- Bottom Interactive Call to Action -->
      <div class="mt-12 p-6 rounded-2xl bg-gradient-to-r from-purple-950/40 via-cyan-950/40 to-slate-950 border border-purple-500/30 text-center">
        <h3 class="text-xl font-black text-white mb-2">Simulate Your Pipeline DAG Online</h3>
        <p class="text-xs sm:text-sm text-slate-300 max-w-xl mx-auto mb-4">
          Before launching local Docker containers, paste your workflow YAML into CIPipelineGraph to inspect job dependencies and verify zero circular cycles.
        </p>
        <a href="/#visualizer" class="inline-flex items-center px-5 py-2.5 rounded-lg bg-purple-500 hover:bg-purple-400 text-slate-950 font-bold text-xs transition shadow-lg shadow-purple-500/20">
          Open In-Browser DAG Visualizer &rarr;
        </a>
      </div>

    </div>
  </article>
</Layout>
